```text
9. testing — 'all clear, proceed' gate
    test the backend in-process, no server, no browser, no real disk.
    seams already exist: DiskPort + ConfigParserPort are ABCs, so fake them.
    what to cover, in risk order:
      - ingestion / numap entity graph (validators, dep ordering, ingest regex)
      - kb state machine (handle_start, domain select, prompt select, hot path)
      - render pipeline (hydration, truncation, hot-prompt resolver, manifest)
      - apply_file_changes (block parsing, deletelist, fence stripping)
    shape:
      - one pytest file or small tests/ dir
      - fixture factories: in-memory disk (dict of path->content), fake cfg parser, canonical workspace
      - fake disk records writes/deletes for assertion
      - the gate is just: run pytest, exit 0 = green light
    out of scope:
      - http server wiring (thin delegation)
      - frontend (display layer)
      - gpu box proxy (pass-through)
```
```text
11. provider model:
    Clanker's system config can declare providers.
    The auth tokens and such would be carried in another file, contained in clanker repo but .gitignored. needs to be safe, anywayy

    a. commercial providers
       - anything that speaks /v1/chat/completions (this is openai's api?)
       - user supplies base_url + api_key (or no key for local)
       - this is the "default" shape, most providers fit here

    b. gpu-box (custom)
       - the tailnet-hosted thing, local GPU
       - adds host-side control: desktop/inference mode switching, raw box management

    c. noprovider public browser gui llm offerings on the free tier
       - basically the user will use the webui to get prompts to clipboard
       - paste those into webui of providers, converse
       - copy replies which are intented for ingestion over to clank webui, paste
```

III. Items under development
```text
1. Add GET /api/repositories to list sibling projects and clanker
    [ ] 'backend/controller.py': Register new GET /api/repositories route returning a JSON array of repository ids
        - Return 200 with application/json
        - Body is a sorted list of directory-name ids
        - Do not verify whether siblings are clanker projects (out of scope)
    [ ] 'backend/adapters/disk_adapter.py': Add list_sibling_repositories() method to the disk adapter
        - Scan the parent directory of clanker_path (the projects dir)
        - Predicate: entry must be a directory, not hidden (no dot prefix), not a symlink
        - Return sorted directory names (alphabetical)
        - clanker is included automatically as a sibling; do not double-add
    [ ] 'backend/core/engine_deps/ports.py': Add list_sibling_repositories() to the DiskPort interface
        - Ensure the controller can call it through the DiskPort abstraction
        - Mark raised exceptions if applicable
```

Backlog tail, Selected item/items:

```text
1. Unify message stats into a single phased footer
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/message.js': Replace separate prefill-bar and performance-footer with one always-present stats line that reformats per phase
        - remove the `.prefill-bar` div from the HTML template entirely
        - repurpose `.performance-footer` as the single stats element; visible from first data tick, not hidden until completion
        - track internal phase state: prefill → reasoning → content → final
        - on first `onPrefill(pp)`: start prefill timer, render running prefill (processed/total, cached, elapsed, tps)
        - on first non-empty `updateReasoning`: freeze prefill section, start reasoning timer, render frozen prefill + running reasoning (est ~tok via chars_per_token, elapsed)
        - on first non-empty `updateContent`: freeze reasoning section, start content timer, render frozen prefill + frozen reasoning + running content
        - on `setPerformanceTimings(timings)`: freeze all, render final with authoritative values (prompt_n, prompt_per_second, predicted_n, predicted_per_second, cache_n)
        - final line appends `mtp X%` only if `timings.draft_n` and `timings.draft_n_accepted` are both present
        - compute `chars_per_token` from a `sentChars` property (set by caller) divided by `prompt_progress.total`
        - use `~` prefix on estimated token counts (reasoning/content running and final split)
        - final reasoning/content token split derived as `predicted_n * (reasoning_chars / total_gen_chars)`
        - remove `hidePrefillBar`, `#hidePrefillBar`, `#prefillState`, prefill-related fields from the element
        - remove `prefill-bar` CSS and DOM references
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/clanker-app.js': Pass sent char count to assistant message before streaming begins
        - compute `totalChars` from `this.messagesBox.getHistory()` (sum of `content.length`)
        - set `assistantMsg.sentChars = totalChars` before the `streamChatCompletion` call
        - no other changes to the streaming callback wiring
```
Backlog tail end
I thought I would make better use of the data, available, and also present it better to the user.

The idea is that we have only one 'stats' elements. while the msg is still streaming, we use the data we have. When the final one ticks, we get the truth and can just use that outright (in my thinking at least)

